IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched2-tribunal`

-- ind-c-tests-sched2: independent tests (author ind-c) of Schedule 2, the Charity Tribunal.  Row ids S2.x-nn are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Schedule 2`

GIVEN appointed IS A DATE
      firstDay IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
      views IS A MAYBE DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE DATE
      reappointed IS A BOOLEAN
      becameMember IS A MAYBE DATE
      before IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
GIVETH AN `Appointment of a member of the tribunal`
`ind-c member appointment` appointed firstDay expires views notice reappointed becameMember before MEANS
    `Appointment of a member of the tribunal` WITH
        `the day of the appointment` IS appointed
        `the first day of the term` IS firstDay
        `the day the term expires` IS expires
        `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable for the position` IS TRUE
        `the person appears to the Minister to have appropriate experience to safeguard the interests of the public and the charitable sector in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS views
        `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS notice
        `the person was serving as a member of the tribunal on the day of the appointment` IS FALSE
        `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS reappointed
        `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS becameMember
        `the service before this appointment` IS before

GIVEN from IS A DATE
      stopped IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of service under the Schedules`
`ind-c service` from stopped MEANS
    `Period of service under the Schedules` WITH `first day of service` IS from, `day service stopped` IS stopped, `as a designated relevant person` IS FALSE

GIVEN given IS A DATE
      effective IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal`
`ind-c member resignation` given effective MEANS
    `Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal` WITH
        `the day the notice was given` IS given
        `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS TRUE
        `the day the resignation takes effect` IS effective

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
`ind-c absence` first last MEANS
    `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` WITH
        `the first day of absence from duties` IS JUST first
        `the last day of absence from duties` IS JUST last
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` IS TRUE
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt` IS FALSE
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness` IS FALSE
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal` IS FALSE

GIVEN bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN
      ill IS A BOOLEAN
      unfit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal`
`ind-c other grounds` bankrupt ill unfit MEANS
    `Grounds for terminating the appointment of a member of the tribunal` WITH
        `the first day of absence from duties` IS NOTHING
        `the last day of absence from duties` IS NOTHING
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` IS FALSE
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt` IS bankrupt
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness` IS ill
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member of the tribunal` IS unfit

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      provided IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Report on the tribunal for a calendar year`
`ind-c tribunal report` year provided MEANS
    `Report on the tribunal for a calendar year` WITH
        `the calendar year` IS year
        `the responsible officer has prepared the report` IS TRUE
        `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister` IS provided
        `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year` IS TRUE
        `the day on which the Minister laid a copy before the States` IS NOTHING
        `the copy was laid as soon as practicable after the Minister received the report` IS TRUE

GIVEN months IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      fine IS A `Fine provided`
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`ind-c penalty` months fine MEANS `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS months, `fine` IS fine

§ `ind-c Schedule 2 paragraph 1 -- appointment`

-- S2.1-01: at least 4, no more than 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 3
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 4
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(1) the number of members of the tribunal is within the limits` 9
-- S2.1-02, S2.1-03: the JAC's views and the 2 weeks' notice, as for the Commissioner
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(2) the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before the appointment` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2032 2 1) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2032 1 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2032 1 14) (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
-- S2.1-04: not more than 6 years
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 2) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
-- S2.1-05: one as chair and another as vice-chair
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` (LIST "Ann", "Bo", "Cy", "Di") (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Bo")
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` (LIST "Ann", "Bo", "Cy", "Di") (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Ann")
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` (LIST "Ann", "Bo", "Cy", "Di") (JUST "Ann") NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(7) one member is designated as the chair and another as the vice-chair` (LIST "Ann", "Bo", "Cy", "Di") (JUST "Ann") (JUST "Zed")
-- S2.1-06 .. S2.1-09: honorary unless the chair, or all, are to be remunerated
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined nothing about remuneration` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States` TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that the chair is to be remunerated by the States` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 1(8) service as a tribunal member is honorary` `the Minister has determined that all the members are to be remunerated by the States` FALSE

§ `ind-c Schedule 2 paragraph 2 -- termination`

-- S2.2-01 (pre-committed ambiguous on the month-end; reading A taken): one month's notice
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member resignation` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 4 15)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member resignation` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 4 14)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) (YMD 2026 2 28)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C` (`ind-c member resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) (YMD 2026 2 28)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C` (`ind-c member resignation` (YMD 2026 1 31) (YMD 2026 3 3)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 3)
-- S2.2-02: absence longer than 8 consecutive weeks (56 days is not; 57 is)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c absence` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 25))
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 8 consecutive weeks` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c absence` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 26))
-- the Commissioner's 4 weeks do not carry over: 29 days' absence is no ground for a tribunal member
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c absence` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29))
-- S2.2-03
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c other grounds` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c other grounds` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c other grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c other grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S2.2-04: not more than 2 weeks after terminating
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 2(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 16)
-- S2.2-05, S2.2-06: twelve years; membership of the States
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(4) the day on which the appointment expires` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) NOTHING NOTHING TRUE NOTHING (LIST (`ind-c service` (YMD 2020 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)))) EQUALS YMD 2032 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(4) the day on which the appointment expires` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c member appointment` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 5 5)) EMPTY) EQUALS YMD 2027 5 5

§ `ind-c Schedule 2 paragraph 3 -- staff and the report`

-- S2.3-01: at least one responsible officer
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 3(2) at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` 0 TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3(2) at least one member of staff is available to the tribunal as the responsible officer` 1 TRUE
-- S2.3-02: the responsible officer assists with administration, not determinations
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 3(2) the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the matter` `a determination by the tribunal`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3(2) the responsible officer is charged with assisting with the matter` `the administration of the tribunal`
-- S2.3-04: the report for 2025 by 30 April 2026
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer provided the Minister with the report in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c tribunal report` 2025 (JUST (YMD 2026 4 30)))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer provided the Minister with the report in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c tribunal report` 2025 (JUST (YMD 2026 5 2)))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer provided the Minister with the report in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c tribunal report` 2025 NOTHING)

§ `ind-c Schedule 2 paragraph 4 -- procedure`

-- S2.4-01 .. S2.4-05: who presides
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation` `at the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation` `absent from the sitting` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the vice-chair`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation` `absent from the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `a member appointed for the purpose by the members present at the sitting`
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation` `at the sitting` `absent from the sitting` EQUALS `the chair`
-- a vacant office: F9.15 A (counts as absent) and B (no answer), by the readings' definitions
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation` `the office is vacant` `at the sitting` EQUALS `the vice-chair`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4(1) the person presiding over a sitting` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.15 is read as B` `the office is vacant` `at the sitting`
-- S2.4-06: the tribunal's own procedure, subject to 4(1) and Regulations
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(2) the tribunal may regulate the matter by its own procedure` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(2) the tribunal may regulate the matter by its own procedure` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(2) the tribunal may regulate the matter by its own procedure` FALSE TRUE
-- S2.4-07: Regulations may create offences up to 2 years and a fine
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c penalty` (JUST 24) `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c penalty` (JUST 36) `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c penalty` NOTHING `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`) (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- the Law states no quorum
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 2 para 4 the quorum of the tribunal is not stated in the Law`
